---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "What is the main goal in IELTS Academic Task 1?",
    answer:
      "The main goal is to describe the key features of the chart, table, map, or process clearly. You do not need to include every detail.",
  },
  {
    question: "Do I need to give my opinion in IELTS Academic Task 1?",
    answer:
      "No. Academic Task 1 is an objective report. You should describe the information, not give personal views about it.",
  },
  {
    question: "What is the most common mistake in IELTS Academic Task 1?",
    answer:
      "A very common mistake is listing numbers without showing the main trends or comparisons. The examiner wants a clear overview, not a data dump.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "IELTS Writing Task 1 Academic Guide", path: "/blog/ielts-writing-task-1-academic-guide/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="IELTS Writing Task 1 Academic Guide | Charts, Tables, Maps and Processes"
  description="A clear IELTS Academic Task 1 guide with overview writing, paragraph structure, and practical advice for describing visuals more effectively."
  type="article"
  keywords="IELTS Writing Task 1 Academic, IELTS chart report, IELTS Task 1 structure, Band 7 IELTS writing"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section guide-article">
    <a class="guide-back-link" href="/blog">Back to blog</a>

    <header class="guide-header">
      <span class="guide-tag ic-eyebrow">IELTS writing guide</span>
      <h1 class="ic-display" style="margin: 0;">IELTS Writing Task 1 Academic guide</h1>
      <div class="guide-meta">
        <span>March 17, 2026</span>
        <span>7 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="guide-lead">
      <p>
        IELTS Academic Task 1 is a report, not an essay. Your job is to identify the key
        features of the visual and describe them clearly. Many students lose marks because
        they try to mention every number instead of showing the main picture.
      </p>
      <p>
        The best reports are selective. They show the important trends, comparisons, and
        stages, then support them with useful details.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-grid guide-grid-2">
      <section class="guide-card">
        <h2 class="ic-display">What this task wants</h2>
        <ul class="guide-list">
          <li>A clear overview of the main trends or features.</li>
          <li>Logical grouping of details.</li>
          <li>Accurate comparisons.</li>
          <li>Objective language with no personal opinion.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-card">
        <h2 class="ic-display">What often lowers the score</h2>
        <ul class="guide-list">
          <li>Too many numbers with no overview.</li>
          <li>The report is organized like a list, not a paragraph plan.</li>
          <li>The writer uses inaccurate comparisons.</li>
          <li>Opinion language appears in the report.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">A simple Task 1 Academic structure</h2>
      <div class="guide-steps">
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Introduction</h3>
            <p>Paraphrase the task in one sentence. Say what the visual shows.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Overview</h3>
            <p>Write the main trend, highest and lowest points, or biggest change without many numbers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Body paragraph 1</h3>
            <p>Group the first set of key details together and compare them clearly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Body paragraph 2</h3>
            <p>Group the remaining important details in a logical way.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">What to notice before you write</h2>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>Which item is highest? Which is lowest?</li>
        <li>What changes the most over time?</li>
        <li>Which items are similar enough to group together?</li>
        <li>What should go in the overview instead of the body?</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">Overview example</h2>
      <div class="guide-example">
        <p>
          <strong>Example overview:</strong> Overall, car ownership increased steadily in
          all three countries, although Canada remained the highest throughout the period
          while Japan had the lowest figures.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-note" style="margin-top: var(--s-3);">
        <p>
          This overview works because it highlights the biggest pattern without filling the
          sentence with exact numbers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">Common mistakes</h2>
      <table class="guide-mistake-table">
        <tr>
          <th>Mistake</th>
          <th>Better move</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Writing only data and no overview.</td>
          <td>State the main trend before you describe the details.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Explaining every number in order.</td>
          <td>Group similar information together instead.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Using opinion phrases like "I think".</td>
          <td>Keep the report factual and objective.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Making inaccurate comparisons.</td>
          <td>Check whether the chart really shows more, less, higher, lower, or a change.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">Next step</h2>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="/blog/ielts-writing-task-1-general-training-letter">
          <strong>Read the General Training letter guide</strong>
          <span>Compare Academic Task 1 report writing with the letter format in GT.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/ai-feedback">
          <strong>Try AI writing feedback</strong>
          <span>Find out whether your overview and comparisons are clear enough.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/ielts/writing">
          <strong>Go to the IELTS writing hub</strong>
          <span>Move to another writing task or a supporting lesson.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="guide-faq">
        {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="card">
            <summary>{item.question}</summary>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <section class="section-sm" style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center;">
    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; margin-bottom: var(--s-5);" />
    <p class="muted">Want a CLB 9 writing system you can actually follow?</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/celpip/writing">Get the system</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
